      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "LDL particles accumulating in your arteries form fatty streaks that can harden and narrow the walls over time, which is the definition of atherosclerosis. This narrowing reduces blood flow and can lead to serious cardiovascular problems. If left untreated, high LDL increases your risk of heart attack and stroke.",
