      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's more of a slow buildup and hardening process rather than an active attack by the LDL itself. Essentially, the LDL gets trapped under the inner lining of the artery wall, triggering an inflammatory response from the body. This inflammation allows cholesterol and other materials to accumulate, leading to the formation of plaque, which physically restricts blood flow.",
